  WHY THE RULE AND THE MANDATED SUBJECT CANNOT DISAGREE, read from the rule
  and the file rather than assumed. The rule's pattern-sources is `$PARAM`
  inside `def $CTRL(..., $PARAM: $TYPE, ...)`, i.e. a method parameter; its
  sink is an s"..."/f"..." interpolation (or a concatenated/built string)
  matching the SQL-keyword regex
  select|delete|insert|create|update|alter|drop. In DiskStore.scala the
  parameter is `blockId`, declared at line 64 in `def put(blockId:
  BlockId)(writeFunc: WritableByteChannel => Unit): Unit`, and the matching
  sink is the interpolation at line 72 inside
  SparkException.internalError(...) - the keyword hit being 'delete'. Source
  and sink are inside ONE method, so the flow crosses no method boundary.


